  "profile_cannot_settle": "the case that motivated ADR-011. church@v0 refuses computed expressions, so `PLUS 7 5` is not measurable here; the 601-ATP figure belongs to manifesto/tools/glyphlib.py, which admitted any expression and argued no domain. See EXP-ADR011-01.",
  "what_these_numbers_do_not_establish": [
    "that normal-form equality is linear in general: this is the cost of obtaining the OBSERVATION normal form on one measured family, and it scaled roughly linearly with the length of the constructor spine F^n(X)",
    "anything about terms outside the admitted domain; normalizing an arbitrary term may be expensive or may not terminate at all",
    "an asymptotic bound of any kind \u2014 these are ATP measurements on one revision and one interpreter, not a complexity result, and nothing in CI protects the shape of the curve",
    "any comparison against in-language equality: the EQN figures in the candidate ADR were measured by a different harness and are cited there, not reproduced here"
  ],
  "what_is_constant": "comparing two ALREADY-OBTAINED addresses is constant in the size of the data, because it compares two 32-byte digests. Obtaining them is the cost measured above."
